#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:73
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "STRICT. `beans create` is not idempotent: it mints a fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing, so re-entering a step duplicates the plan instead of no-op'ing. In the qou folio an unguarded re-run produced 14,688 duplicate beans — 92% of every open bean — which starved the idle-backlog policy of signal and collided with 15 real ids."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only task in this diagram with no `cat-harness.processes:bean` op at all — every other terminal action here writes something, and this one's entire job is to write nothing to a bean it does not own, ending the lifecycle at End_NotYours rather than at the completion Lane_Agent reaches for its own beans."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:127
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The performer's judgement on the work, and one of three recorded endings. `done`: complete it only when no todo is unchecked, with a summary of what changed. `not wanted`: set it `scrapped` with a 'Reasons for Scrapping' section — never delete. `blocked`: record what it waits on with `--blocked-by`, say what would unblock it, and return it to `todo`, because an in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The whole life of a work-plan item, and the rules that make one agent's bean legible to another: check before you create, claim before you work, keep the body current as you go, and end it in a state that says why. You are in this process the moment durable work is identified — which is before the first tool call, not after the work is done. The second lane exists because a bean you did not open is not yours to close: coordination replaces a decision you are not entitled to make. The one irreversible thing is refused outright. Unwanted work is SCRAPPED with its reasons, never deleted, because a scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end while a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident."
msgstr ""

